    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nI would explain Qualification in plain language first, then give the technical detail that distinguishes it from nearby concepts. The practical anchor is: Use discovery questions to confirm business need, fit, decision process, timing, and a credible path to value before forecasting the opportunity.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can communicate the concept clearly at an interview pace and adjust the depth when the interviewer asks a follow-up.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Give a one-sentence definition: Qualification determines whether an opportunity has a credible need, fit, authority, timing, and path to purchase.\n2. Explain one important behavior or distinction.\n3. Use the example to make it concrete: Use discovery questions to confirm business need, fit, decision process, timing, and a credible path to value before forecasting the opportunity.\n4. Finish with the limitation: A more disciplined process improves focus and forecast quality but can slow conversations if it is applied as a rigid checklist instead of a decision aid.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would keep the first answer concise, then wait for the interviewer to signal whether they want internals. If they go deeper, I would expand the mechanism and trade-offs rather than repeating the definition.\n\n**Example :**\nUse discovery questions to confirm business need, fit, decision process, timing, and a credible path to value before forecasting the opportunity.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA customer opportunity may use Qualification when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, use discovery questions to confirm business need, fit, decision process, timing, and a credible path to value before forecasting the opportunity. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Qualification as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Qualification.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nPractice saying {c} aloud in your own words. A technically correct answer is weaker if you cannot explain it without reading a script.",
