    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nA sales pipeline is the set of active opportunities and their stages, values, and expected next steps.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can define Pipeline accurately and explain what it changes in practice. The interviewer can then probe the boundary conditions, alternatives, or failure cases.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Start with the definition: A sales pipeline is the set of active opportunities and their stages, values, and expected next steps.\n2. Use a concrete case: Review pipeline by stage, age, next step, and evidence so weak opportunities are not treated the same as committed deals.\n3. Keep the explanation tied to the behavior in the question.\n4. Mention the main limitation or trade-off: A more disciplined process improves focus and forecast quality but can slow conversations if it is applied as a rigid checklist instead of a decision aid.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would define Pipeline first, then explain the behavior that matters in practice. I would use the concrete example to make the idea easy to visualize and finish with the main limitation.\n\n**Example :**\nReview pipeline by stage, age, next step, and evidence so weak opportunities are not treated the same as committed deals.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA customer opportunity may use Pipeline when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, review pipeline by stage, age, next step, and evidence so weak opportunities are not treated the same as committed deals. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Pipeline as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Pipeline.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nFor Pipeline, give the definition first and then one consequence. That makes it clear you understand the concept instead of only recognizing the name.",
