    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nThe usual flow for Composition is to start with the inputs or conditions, apply the behavior described here, and verify the resulting state. Composition builds an object from collaborating objects and is often preferred when behavior should be assembled rather than inherited.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis tests whether you understand the mechanism and can explain a sequence, not just the end result.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Establish the starting condition.\n2. Apply the mechanism: Composition builds an object from collaborating objects and is often preferred when behavior should be assembled rather than inherited.\n3. Verify the result using the concrete case: A checkout service can receive a tax calculator and payment gateway as collaborators instead of inheriting from them; the service is assembled from parts with separate responsibilities.\n4. Watch the trade-off or failure condition: For Composition, the useful benefit has to be weighed against the extra complexity, maintenance, or cost introduced by the approach.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nWalk through the normal sequence in order. Explain what changes at each important step, then mention how you would verify the result and what you would inspect if the operation failed.\n\n**Example :**\nA checkout service can receive a tax calculator and payment gateway as collaborators instead of inheriting from them; the service is assembled from parts with separate responsibilities.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nAn application being built or maintained by a junior engineer may use Composition when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, a checkout service can receive a tax calculator and payment gateway as collaborators instead of inheriting from them; the service is assembled from parts with separate responsibilities. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Composition as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Composition.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nExplain the state change behind the steps. That is more useful than listing commands or buzzwords.",
